# Unified Update System

Meridian uses a single update flow. One app version = one Wine engine snapshot. Users never deal with separate app and engine updates.

## CRITICAL: Engine/App Separation Principle

**The app NEVER compensates for engine deficiencies. The engine NEVER compensates for app deficiencies.**

Every time a bug is found that involves the engine or app working around each other's problems:

1. **Fix the root layer.** If the engine is broken (missing file, wrong layout, bad DLL), fix `release-engine.sh` and publish a new engine release. If the app is broken, fix the app.
2. **Publish the fixed engine immediately.** Run `bash Scripts/release-engine.sh` to push the corrected engine to GitHub Releases.
3. **Clear the broken installed engine.** Delete `~/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/engine/` so the app is forced to download the fresh, correct engine.
4. **Verify end-to-end** with the new engine before closing the issue.

**Never:**
- Add app-level workarounds for missing engine files (e.g. manually copying DLLs when `wineboot --update` fails because `wine.inf` is absent)
- Suppress engine errors to make the app appear to work
- Patch around a known engine packaging defect without also fixing the packaging

**Always:**
- When a packaging defect is identified in the engine, fix `release-engine.sh` first
- Add a validation `die()` in `release-engine.sh` so the same defect cannot ship again
- Publish a new engine release before verifying any app-side fix
- Test against the published engine, not a locally-patched state

### Engine Release Checklist (run every time a packaging fix is made)

```bash
# 1. Fix the root issue in Scripts/release-engine.sh
# 2. Publish the new engine
bash Scripts/release-engine.sh            # auto-increments version (e.g. v1.0.4-engine)

# 3. Clear the broken installed engine on the dev machine
rm -rf ~/Library/Application\ Support/com.meridian.app/engine/
defaults delete com.meridian.app lastPrefixEngineTag 2>/dev/null || true

# 4. Clean build and run the app — it will auto-download the new engine on launch
```

---

## How It Works

- `AppUpdateChecker` (`Meridian/Engine/AppUpdateChecker.swift`) queries `https://api.github.com/repos/{engineRepoSlug}/releases`, filters by tag suffix to separate app vs engine releases, and compares against installed versions.
- On every launch, `MeridianApp` compares `AppSettings.lastLaunchAppVersion` to the current version. If changed and the engine is already installed, it silently triggers `EngineDownloader` in the background.
- Settings → Updates tab shows current Meridian version, installed engine tag, update status, release notes, and download controls.

## In-App Update Flows

### Engine update (Settings → Updates → "Download Engine vX.Y.Z")
- `EngineDownloader.download(onComplete:)` fetches the latest `-engine` tagged release from the GitHub API, downloads the `.tar.gz`, and extracts it to `~/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/engine/`.
- On completion, the `onComplete` closure runs `engine.detect()` then `updateChecker.clearEngineUpdate(newTag:)` to sync the installed tag and dismiss the update UI.
- `EngineDownloader.state` drives the button UI: `.downloading(progress:)`, `.extracting`, `.complete`, `.failed`.

### App update (Settings → Updates → "Download & Install vX.Y.Z")
- `AppUpdateChecker.downloadAndInstallUpdate()` downloads the `.dmg` asset from the release, mounts it via `hdiutil attach`, copies the `.app` bundle over the running app, then relaunches via `open -n -a` and calls `NSApp.terminate`.
- Falls back to opening the browser release page if no `.dmg` asset is attached.
- `AppUpdateChecker.appUpdateState` drives button UI: `.downloading(progress:)`, `.installing`, `.readyToRelaunch`, `.failed`.

## End users vs maintainers

- **End users** do **not** need CrossOver. The only supported runtime is the bundled engine downloaded from GitHub Releases. There is no CrossOver fallback in `WineEngine.detect()`. Meridian is fully self-contained.
- **Maintainers** must have CrossOver Preview installed at `/Applications/CrossOver Preview.app`. Running `release-engine.sh` copies Wine, DXMT, DXVK, and GPTK from CX Preview into the engine tarball. The tarball is uploaded to GitHub Releases and auto-downloaded by end users.

## Developer Release Workflow

```
1. Fix Scripts/release-engine.sh if there is a packaging issue
2. bash Scripts/release-engine.sh        # publishes vX.Y.Z-engine tag
3. Clear installed engine: rm -rf ~/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/engine/
4. Clean build the app and run — verify end-to-end with the published engine
5. Bump MARKETING_VERSION in Xcode
6. Build → sign → notarize → publish .dmg to GitHub Releases as vX.Y.Z
```

Engine releases are tagged `vX.Y.Z-engine`. App releases are tagged `vX.Y.Z`. The update checker uses the `-engine` suffix to distinguish them.

`release-engine.sh` writes `wine/meridian-engine-version.txt` into the archive. `WineEngine.engineVersion` reads this file and surfaces it in Settings → Updates.

## Engine Package Requirements

The engine tarball (`meridian-engine-arm64.tar.gz`) MUST contain:

| Path | Purpose | Missing causes |
|------|---------|----------------|
| `wine/bin/wine64` | Wine loader | Engine not detected |
| `wine/bin/wineserver` | Wine IPC server | All Wine operations fail |
| `wine/share/wine/nls/*.nls` | NLS locale tables | Wineserver aborts |
| `wine/share/wine/wine.inf` | Prefix creation/update spec | `wineboot --init` and `wineboot --update` fail — DLL symlinks in prefix become stale after engine upgrade, causing `STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND` (exit 53) |
| `wine/lib/wine/x86_64-unix/winemetal.so` | DXMT Metal bridge | DirectX 11 → Metal path broken |
| `wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows/d3d11.dll` | DXMT D3D11 | DirectX 11 → Metal path broken |
| `wine/meridian-engine-version.txt` | Version tag | Engine version undetectable in Settings |

`release-engine.sh` validates all of the above with `die()` checks. If a new required file is identified, add both the copy step AND the validation check to the script.

**The engine is built from CX Wine (CrossOver Preview).** CX Wine is LGPL 2.1 — legally redistributable. It includes all CodeWeavers patches (DXMT Metal APIs, Steam compat, Rosetta2 thunks, Security.framework TLS) plus `ntdll.__wine_unix_call` which CX's d3d12.dll requires for D3D12/GPTK support. `release-engine.sh` copies Wine, DXMT, DXVK, and GPTK from CrossOver Preview into the engine tarball. End users never need CrossOver installed.

- `Gcenx/winecx` — stopped publishing after Wine 8.0.1 (Feb 2024), do NOT use
- `Gcenx/macOS_Wine_builds` (wine-devel) — lacks `ntdll.__wine_unix_call` needed by CX d3d12.dll. Custom bridge (`Scripts/d3d12-bridge/`) exists as a future option if ever needed.
- `wine-staging` — may introduce regressions, do NOT use

## Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `Meridian/Engine/AppUpdateChecker.swift` | `@Observable @MainActor` update checker + app DMG installer |
| `Meridian/Engine/EngineDownloader.swift` | Downloads and extracts engine archives |
| `Meridian/App/MeridianApp.swift` | Injects `updateChecker`; triggers background engine refresh on version change |
| `Meridian/Models/AppSettings.swift` | `lastUpdateCheck` (rate-limit) + `lastLaunchAppVersion` + `lastPrefixEngineTag` (upgrade detection) |
| `Meridian/Views/Settings/SettingsView.swift` | Updates tab — `UpdatesSettingsTab`, `EngineUpdateSection`, diagnostics section |
| `Meridian/Engine/WinePrefix.swift` | `refreshSystemDLLs(engine:engineTag:)` — runs `wineboot --update` on engine version change |
| `Scripts/release-engine.sh` | Developer script — packages Wine + embeds version file + validates all required files |

## Important Constraints

- Do NOT add separate "engine update" and "app update" buttons that break the unified model. They may appear separately in Settings, but both are driven by a single `checkNow()` call.
- `AppUpdateChecker` has no external package dependencies — consistent with the rest of the codebase (`dependencies: []`).
- The rate limit for background checks is 86,400 seconds (24 hours), stored in `AppSettings.lastUpdateCheck`.
- Engine auto-refresh only fires when `engine.isReady` is true (engine already installed). It never interferes with a fresh install going through `EngineSetupView`.
- After a successful engine download, ALWAYS call `updateChecker.clearEngineUpdate(newTag: engine.engineVersion)` in the `onComplete` closure to dismiss the update UI. Omitting this causes the "update available" banner to persist after installation.
- `WinePrefix.refreshSystemDLLs()` uses only `wineboot --update` — NO app-level DLL copying fallbacks. If `wineboot --update` fails, the error surfaces clearly so the engine packaging is fixed, not masked.
